1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,780
They say once you learn how to ride a bike, you never forget.
人们说一旦你学会骑自行车，就一辈子都不会忘。

2
00:00:04,780 --> 00:00:14,240
Most of us learnt when we were kids, and many still strap on our helmets, put our feet on the pedals, and shoot off for a ride around the streets.
我们大多数人都是小时候学会骑车的，现在还有不少人会戴上头盔，蹬上脚踏板，骑着车在街道上疾驰。

3
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:25,410
In recent times, cycling has seen a boost in popularity, so the question is, what makes it so appealing to people to straddle their bikes once again?
近年来，骑行的受欢迎程度大幅提升，那么问题来了，是什么让人们再次热衷于骑上自行车呢？

4
00:00:25,410 --> 00:00:28,830
First, let’s look at the health benefits.
首先我们来看看骑行对健康的益处。

5
00:00:28,830 --> 00:00:33,950
Cycling can improve your cardiovascular health and burn excess body fat.
骑行能够改善心血管健康，燃烧体内多余脂肪。

6
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:40,940
Strengthening your leg muscles in your calves and thighs helps to increase your potential torque and cadence.
强化小腿和大腿部位的腿部肌肉，有助于提升骑行扭矩和踏频的潜力。

7
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:45,690
And cycling’s benefits aren’t just physical, but mental as well.
而且骑行带来的好处不止体现在身体上，对心理健康也大有裨益。

8
00:00:45,690 --> 00:00:50,600
A long ride in the countryside could help you to clear your mind, or de-stress.
在乡间长途骑行，可以帮助你理清思绪、释放压力。

9
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:57,570
But it’s not only about your body and mind – there are also some plus sides for your wallet’s health.
但骑行的好处可不止于身心层面，对钱包来说也是一大福音。

10
00:00:57,570 --> 00:01:01,900
Cycling can be a great way to commute or get about town.
骑行是通勤或在市区出行的绝佳方式。

11
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:06,130
By cycling, you save money on fuel or train fares.
骑车出行可以省下燃油费或火车票钱。

12
00:01:06,130 --> 00:01:16,120
If you do drive into work, sometimes finding somewhere to park can be a nightmare, whereas finding somewhere to chain your bike up can be much simpler.
如果开车上班，有时候找停车位会是一场噩梦，而找地方锁自行车则要简单得多。

13
00:01:16,120 --> 00:01:23,590
Then, on the train, there are changes at stations and other commuters speaking loudly on their phones to deal with.
坐火车的话，还得应对换乘以及其他通勤者大声打电话的干扰。

14
00:01:23,590 --> 00:01:26,840
Cyclists face neither of these issues.
骑行者则不会遇到这两种麻烦。

15
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:33,020
And if you’re worried about safety, there are designated cycle lanes in many major cities.
如果你担心安全问题，许多大城市都设有专用自行车道。

16
00:01:33,020 --> 00:01:40,990
Wearing high-visibility clothing, sometimes referred to as ‘hi-vis’, is another way to improve your safety when cycling on the roads.
穿上高能见度服装（有时被称为“反光服”），也是提升道路骑行安全性的另一种方法。

17
00:01:40,990 --> 00:01:44,600
Finally, cycling can also be good for the environment.
最后，骑行对环境也有益处。

18
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:47,590
It can help you to reduce your carbon footprint.
它能帮助你减少碳足迹。

19
00:01:47,590 --> 00:01:53,250
Not pumping out fumes into the atmosphere is better for the planet and your own environment.
不会向大气中排放尾气，无论是对地球还是对周边环境来说，都是一件好事。

20
00:01:53,250 --> 00:02:05,260
So, whether people want to cycle for their health, getting about town, their wallet, the environment, or a combination of all of them – the popularity of cycling is on the rise.
所以，无论人们是为了健康、出行、省钱、环保，还是兼而有之，骑行的热度都在持续攀升。
